WEBVTT

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:15.766
Captain's diary. Star date,

00:00:15.816 --> 00:00:18.986
Lrrr and Ndnd's 63rd anniversary.

00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:21.363
Planet Express has been hired to cater

00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:25.075
a vow renewal ceremony
on Omicron Persei 8.

00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:27.494
Not what I thought
I'd be doing at this age.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.538
Mr. Professor! Fuel status?

00:00:29.538 --> 00:00:32.666
If I'm reading this correctly,
we're underwater.

00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:34.376
You're not reading it correctly.

00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:36.628
Mr. Bender. Wedding cake readout?

00:00:36.628 --> 00:00:38.797
Frosting at maximum cream-cheesiness!

00:00:38.797 --> 00:00:40.424
All systems tasty!

00:00:40.424 --> 00:00:43.635
Medical officer Zoidberg.
Are you reaching for the cake?

00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:45.345
Affirmative, Captain.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.346
Ow!

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.224
Stick to fish flakes,
you overgrown sea monkey!

00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:52.436
All parameters nominal,
but stay sharp, crew.

00:00:52.436 --> 00:00:54.396
I don't know why, but I have a feeling

00:00:54.396 --> 00:00:56.899
something's not quite right.

00:00:56.899 --> 00:00:58.984
Everything's fine, Leela.

00:00:58.984 --> 00:01:01.612
We're the best delivery/catering service

00:01:01.612 --> 00:01:03.739
in the galaxy. Right, team?

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:06.366
Damn straight!

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.951
Aw, thanks.

00:01:07.951 --> 00:01:10.913
You always know how
to make me feel better,

00:01:10.913 --> 00:01:13.624
Fry.
- That's what I'm here for, honey.

00:01:13.624 --> 00:01:14.625
dramatic sting

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:17.628
theme song playing

00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.126
Is that Crab Rangoon?

00:01:58.126 --> 00:02:00.295
No, he's Dr. Zoidberg.

00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:02.089
"FRY": Congratulations, sir.

00:02:02.089 --> 00:02:04.633
May I offer you some
sparkling victim juice?

00:02:07.636 --> 00:02:11.139
Here. Place my lead-lined overcape
in the Closet of Heavy Things.

00:02:13.058 --> 00:02:14.309
I love my job.

00:02:14.309 --> 00:02:18.272
timpani drum version of
Bridal Chorus by Wagner

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.817
Belligerent reptiles,
we are gathered here

00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:25.779
under the watchful eye of Jvvv,
God of the Omicronians...

00:02:25.779 --> 00:02:26.947
Hey there.

00:02:26.947 --> 00:02:30.450
...to bear witness as Lrrr and Ndnd

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.578
renew their wedding vows,

00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:35.747
expressing their most personal feelings.

00:02:35.747 --> 00:02:36.957
Wrong!

00:02:36.957 --> 00:02:40.377
Ndnd got them from
an inspirational placemat.

00:02:40.377 --> 00:02:42.713
It was a quality placemat!

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:46.008
Ndnd, you look just as you did

00:02:46.008 --> 00:02:49.052
the night I met you on
the hairy hills of B'dnkdnk,

00:02:49.052 --> 00:02:52.347
your dress covered in the blood
of three B'dnkian warriors.

00:02:52.347 --> 00:02:55.100
You took me in your arms
and ate the morsel

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.977
of B'dnkian entrail

00:02:56.977 --> 00:02:58.770
lodged in my cleavage.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.731
It was delicious.

00:03:00.731 --> 00:03:03.233
Hey, you got any, uh,
B'dnkian entrail on that tray?

00:03:03.233 --> 00:03:05.777
No, but we have
lettuce-wrapped cucumbers,

00:03:05.777 --> 00:03:07.154
which are even grosser.

00:03:07.905 --> 00:03:10.574
Can you stop eating for one second?

00:03:10.574 --> 00:03:12.743
If you want me to not eat,

00:03:12.743 --> 00:03:14.786
then you should have done the cooking!

00:03:14.786 --> 00:03:16.038
Oh snap!

00:03:16.038 --> 00:03:18.665
Having completed the sacred vows,

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:22.127
the groom will now crush
the skull of his father-in-law.

00:03:22.127 --> 00:03:23.837
If it please the Lord?

00:03:23.837 --> 00:03:25.756
Oh yeah, I love that kinda stuff.

00:03:25.923 --> 00:03:29.718
Hava Nagila playing

00:03:29.718 --> 00:03:31.720
Molotov!

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.728
Now, kiss the bride
and come out fighting.

00:03:48.237 --> 00:03:51.406
Why do I have to use the hook?
I hate the hook.

00:03:51.406 --> 00:03:55.035
You managed to capture me
with it at our first wedding.

00:03:55.035 --> 00:03:56.787
You weren't the intended target.

00:03:56.787 --> 00:03:59.957
Oh, I just love it when
they dance the horta.

00:03:59.957 --> 00:04:01.833
Care to join me?

00:04:09.132 --> 00:04:11.969
As best man,
I'd like to say a few words

00:04:11.969 --> 00:04:14.304
about my dear friend Lrrr.

00:04:14.304 --> 00:04:17.391
Keep it clean.
My father's crushed skull is here.

00:04:17.391 --> 00:04:20.435
Intelligent, loyal, brave,

00:04:20.435 --> 00:04:22.104
a great leader!

00:04:22.104 --> 00:04:23.855
But enough about me.

00:04:25.857 --> 00:04:27.818
Stick to the script.

00:04:29.903 --> 00:04:33.699
And now for the tossing of the bouquet.

00:04:34.825 --> 00:04:37.411
Uh, nobody invited the help.

00:04:37.411 --> 00:04:40.080
Nobody invited me
to kick your ass either,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.040
yet here we are. Hi-ya!

00:04:42.874 --> 00:04:44.751
Flowers in the hole!

00:04:47.879 --> 00:04:49.881
The glory is mine!

00:04:59.474 --> 00:05:02.269
Now, this part I don't like.

00:05:09.109 --> 00:05:11.069
I wonder what I should bake next.

00:05:11.069 --> 00:05:13.739
Hey, Fry, you ever wanted to be in a pie?

00:05:13.739 --> 00:05:16.867
Anything for you, buddy.
Point me to the crust, and I'll be there.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.580
That takes care of the dishes.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:23.790
You want me to get started
on the floors, Hermes?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.751
Or should I scrub down Dr. Zoidberg?

00:05:25.751 --> 00:05:27.002
Scrub-a-dub-dub!

00:05:27.002 --> 00:05:28.670
How are you so energetic?

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:31.214
Oh, I'll never get tired of this job.

00:05:32.466 --> 00:05:34.426
I have the best life ever.

00:05:34.426 --> 00:05:35.719
That's our Fry.

00:05:35.719 --> 00:05:37.512
It sure is.

00:05:37.512 --> 00:05:39.598
It most definitely is.

00:05:44.603 --> 00:05:46.063
Twenty-three years earlier,

00:05:46.063 --> 00:05:47.522
the crew was recuperating

00:05:47.522 --> 00:05:50.025
from a grueling mission to planet Amazonia

00:05:50.025 --> 00:05:53.987
where Fry had sustained extensive
snu-snu-related injuries.

00:05:53.987 --> 00:05:56.782
What a relief
to be back on Earth,

00:05:56.782 --> 00:05:59.243
where nobody wants
to have snu-snu with me.

00:05:59.243 --> 00:06:02.663
My pelvis and I
could really use a vacation.

00:06:02.663 --> 00:06:04.957
Any chance I can get
some time off, Professor?

00:06:04.957 --> 00:06:07.960
I'm not sure.
How will we stay in business

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.587
without our ace delivery boy?

00:06:10.587 --> 00:06:12.881
Extremely easily.

00:06:14.258 --> 00:06:15.634
See you in two weeks!

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.719
Enjoy Amazonia!

00:06:17.719 --> 00:06:19.513
Come on. Let's get a temp dimwit

00:06:19.513 --> 00:06:21.557
to replace our permanent one.

00:06:28.397 --> 00:06:30.691
- I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:30.691 --> 00:06:33.735
I don't know what happened
to our office manager Evans.

00:06:33.735 --> 00:06:35.237
Is that him?

00:06:36.113 --> 00:06:37.114
Maybe?

00:06:37.114 --> 00:06:38.782
Uh, how can I help you?

00:06:38.782 --> 00:06:40.909
One of our workers is on vacation,

00:06:40.909 --> 00:06:42.452
so we'll need to hire a temp.

00:06:42.452 --> 00:06:44.079
We've got whatever you need.

00:06:44.079 --> 00:06:46.790
Secretary, jockey, lion tamer,

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.625
bowling shoe spray technician.

00:06:48.625 --> 00:06:50.544
What exactly are you looking for?

00:06:50.544 --> 00:06:53.463
Well, let's see.
It's a thankless job.

00:06:53.463 --> 00:06:54.840
He'll never be thanked.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.342
- Any skills?
- Absolutely not!

00:06:57.342 --> 00:07:00.178
I'll need to berate him
for being incompetent!

00:07:00.178 --> 00:07:02.347
Then, I've got just the schlep for you.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.688
Frank, you're going to be working
at Planet Express for two weeks.

00:07:09.688 --> 00:07:12.274
Lucky me. Let's just get it over with.

00:07:12.274 --> 00:07:15.319
Perfect! He sounds very berate-able.

00:07:19.573 --> 00:07:21.450
I'll introduce you to the group.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.869
Uh, what was your name again?
- Frank.

00:07:24.369 --> 00:07:26.872
Everyone, please welcome our new temp.

00:07:26.872 --> 00:07:29.041
This is, uh...
- Frank.

00:07:29.041 --> 00:07:31.418
Hi, Frank. Tell us about yourself.

00:07:31.418 --> 00:07:33.962
I have no characteristics
and people forget me

00:07:33.962 --> 00:07:35.297
as soon as I leave the room.

00:07:35.297 --> 00:07:37.007
And sometimes before that.

00:07:37.007 --> 00:07:40.135
That's ridiculous! Um...

00:07:40.135 --> 00:07:42.471
Frank. Is this my cubicle?

00:07:42.471 --> 00:07:46.225
No, that's an empty space
between three stacks of boxes.

00:07:46.225 --> 00:07:48.977
Well, I guess I'll stand in there.

00:07:48.977 --> 00:07:50.103
Come out, please.

00:07:50.103 --> 00:07:52.648
You're gonna be traveling around
delivering things.

00:07:52.648 --> 00:07:54.608
- Yeah, right.
- Right.

00:07:54.608 --> 00:07:56.652
Wait, seriously? Traveling?

00:07:56.652 --> 00:07:59.071
I-I've never been anywhere before.

00:07:59.071 --> 00:08:01.031
Why not? There's a tube station

00:08:01.031 --> 00:08:03.325
that'll take you to Paris for five cents.

00:08:03.325 --> 00:08:06.245
I don't have time for that.
Temping is a full-time job.

00:08:55.252 --> 00:08:57.129
Those are beautiful!

00:08:57.129 --> 00:09:00.757
Thanks a lot,
uh, I wanna say Dave?

00:09:00.757 --> 00:09:03.510
Frank. I'm the temp.
I've been here two weeks.

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:05.304
The best two weeks of my life.

00:09:05.304 --> 00:09:07.472
Ah! That's the frittata.

00:09:07.472 --> 00:09:08.849
I hope you're all hungry.

00:09:09.892 --> 00:09:12.352
Ugh! He's so enthusiastic.

00:09:12.352 --> 00:09:14.855
I can't stand his toxic positivity.

00:09:14.855 --> 00:09:18.275
He likes everyone, even me!
It's pathetic.

00:09:18.275 --> 00:09:22.195
Well, he's no Fry,
but at least Fry will be back tomorrow.

00:09:22.195 --> 00:09:25.449
Wow. Fry's not even here
and you remember his name?

00:09:25.449 --> 00:09:28.785
He must be quite a guy.
- Sorry, that was rude.

00:09:28.785 --> 00:09:32.581
You've done a good job, uh... you.

00:09:32.581 --> 00:09:36.376
And since it's your last day,
let's make it a good one. Right, gang?

00:09:36.376 --> 00:09:37.878
- Sure.
- Why not?

00:09:37.878 --> 00:09:39.171
Who the hell is he?

00:09:51.225 --> 00:09:53.769
Hello! Welcome to the liberry.

00:09:53.769 --> 00:09:55.395
You called for a dump job?

00:09:55.395 --> 00:09:57.564
Oh, yes. We had a water main break,

00:09:57.564 --> 00:10:00.567
and it damaged some of the books.
And by some, I mean

00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:02.444
all 2.6 million.

00:10:02.444 --> 00:10:05.405
You're throwing out
all the liberry books?

00:10:05.405 --> 00:10:09.368
Look, nobody's checked
a book out since 2029.

00:10:09.368 --> 00:10:12.621
It was this one.
- A novelization of the TikTok video

00:10:12.621 --> 00:10:16.583
"Peanut Butter Eating Dog
Lip Syncs to Olivia Rodrigo."

00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:18.585
Ooh! I'd watch that.

00:10:18.585 --> 00:10:20.420
It's a book. You'd read it.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.631
No, I wouldn't.

00:10:26.468 --> 00:10:29.763
Where are we gonna dump
these disgusting books? The ocean?

00:10:29.763 --> 00:10:33.433
Certainly not!
It's been illegal to dump hazardous waste

00:10:33.433 --> 00:10:35.894
in the ocean for over a year now.

00:10:35.894 --> 00:10:39.273
We'll head for that book containment
facility on Dalton-B.

00:10:39.273 --> 00:10:41.817
It's a small planet in
the Barnzan Nobula.

00:10:49.783 --> 00:10:52.578
Watch out for flying
purple paper eaters!

00:10:52.578 --> 00:10:55.664
My travel-sized filing cabinet!

00:10:59.668 --> 00:11:02.296
Ew! I got book on me!

00:11:03.505 --> 00:11:05.924
So weird that reading
used to be a thing.

00:11:07.509 --> 00:11:09.177
Well, that's the last of 'em.

00:11:09.177 --> 00:11:11.221
Let's get outta here before some dork says

00:11:11.221 --> 00:11:13.473
trashing books is a travesty.

00:11:17.185 --> 00:11:19.271
Well, that's the last of 'em.

00:11:19.271 --> 00:11:21.315
Hey, guys? Guys!

00:11:21.315 --> 00:11:23.525
The ship is abandoning us!

00:11:23.525 --> 00:11:24.526
Guys?

00:11:24.526 --> 00:11:26.778
Oh.

00:11:31.491 --> 00:11:34.703
Ugh. I'm gonna go wash
the book smell out of my hair.

00:11:37.331 --> 00:11:39.333
I'm home from my vacation!

00:11:39.333 --> 00:11:42.920
Did I miss anything?
- Only a delivery to book hell.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.923
We're just lucky we made it back
without reading anything.

00:11:45.923 --> 00:11:48.133
We did all make it back, right?

00:11:48.133 --> 00:11:50.969
Well, let's see. There's me, Bender,

00:11:50.969 --> 00:11:54.181
and some other people...
We're good.

00:11:54.181 --> 00:11:56.475
Five, 6, 7, 8.

00:11:56.475 --> 00:11:59.019
All eight crew members present
and accounted for.

00:12:00.604 --> 00:12:02.397
Ayup. Mm-hmm.

00:12:02.397 --> 00:12:05.150
I can get through this.
I'm a temp, dammit.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:07.569
I'm sure they'll be back soon.

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:11.615
Twenty-three years later,
the crew was about to depart

00:12:11.615 --> 00:12:14.660
for the wedding ceremony
on Omicron Persei 8.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.329
The one you saw earlier. That one.

00:12:18.455 --> 00:12:22.000
Will you quit slacking off, Fry?
I need more whipped frosting!

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.169
Sorry. I'm just kinda worn out.

00:12:31.176 --> 00:12:33.303
I guess work's been catching up to me.

00:12:33.303 --> 00:12:36.390
Sometimes, I wonder if I was
cut out to be a whatever I am.

00:12:36.390 --> 00:12:39.226
You have been burning
the blunt at both ends, mon.

00:12:39.226 --> 00:12:42.104
After this wedding cake delivery,
you should take a vacation.

00:12:42.104 --> 00:12:43.605
When's the last time you took one?

00:12:43.605 --> 00:12:47.442
Twenty-three years ago,
after that horrific snu-snu incident.

00:12:47.442 --> 00:12:51.071
If Fry takes a vacation,
we'll have to get someone to fill in.

00:12:51.071 --> 00:12:53.782
Why? We didn't get anyone last time.

00:12:53.782 --> 00:12:55.158
Or did we?

00:12:55.158 --> 00:12:57.578
Oh, right. The temp!

00:12:57.578 --> 00:12:59.746
What's-his-name!
- He had a name?

00:12:59.746 --> 00:13:01.456
Even I looked down on him.

00:13:04.376 --> 00:13:08.005
He went with us on that trip to dump
those old liberry books,

00:13:08.005 --> 00:13:10.882
and then... and then!

00:13:10.882 --> 00:13:12.551
dramatic sting

00:13:12.551 --> 00:13:15.095
- What?
- I'm sure he's fine.

00:13:15.095 --> 00:13:17.514
We'll just swing by on the way
to the wedding

00:13:17.514 --> 00:13:19.433
and pick up his corpse.

00:13:24.396 --> 00:13:27.774
Yuck! This place is even
grosser than I remembered.

00:13:27.774 --> 00:13:30.485
I don't see him. Let's just go.

00:13:30.485 --> 00:13:32.321
Y-You came back.

00:13:32.321 --> 00:13:34.781
I...

00:13:34.781 --> 00:13:36.700
I thought you'd forgotten about me.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:39.202
Oh no. We could never forget...

00:13:40.579 --> 00:13:42.080
- Frank!

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.332
- Of course!
- Sounds right.

00:13:43.332 --> 00:13:45.626
It was on the tip of my tendrils!

00:13:45.626 --> 00:13:48.962
My heavens. It's been 23 years!

00:13:48.962 --> 00:13:50.422
What did you eat?

00:13:50.422 --> 00:13:53.008
Books! Book sandwiches, book soup,

00:13:53.008 --> 00:13:55.052
scrambled books with fly larvae!

00:13:55.052 --> 00:13:57.012
Ew, books!

00:14:00.182 --> 00:14:02.226
The shower's through there.

00:14:02.226 --> 00:14:05.145
There's plenty of soap
and toothpaste in Fry's cubby.

00:14:05.145 --> 00:14:06.521
He never uses them.

00:14:20.244 --> 00:14:23.330
It's just as itchy as
I dreamed it would be.

00:14:28.043 --> 00:14:30.712
Hey, coworkers!
Shouldn't we be heading off

00:14:30.712 --> 00:14:32.339
to deliver that wedding cake?

00:14:32.339 --> 00:14:34.508
Yeah. We just need to wait for Fry.

00:14:34.508 --> 00:14:35.634
He's not back yet.

00:14:35.634 --> 00:14:38.637
Yes, I am. I'm right here...

00:14:45.894 --> 00:14:48.605
Ah, Fry! There you are!

00:14:48.605 --> 00:14:51.233
Let's go already!

00:14:56.071 --> 00:14:58.490
Finally, a use for the Bible.

00:14:58.490 --> 00:14:59.866
Hey, wait.

00:14:59.866 --> 00:15:03.704
Why hast thou forsaken me?!

00:15:08.917 --> 00:15:10.335
- Hey, Leela.

00:15:10.335 --> 00:15:13.088
After work, you wanna binge
some Hungry-Man streaming dinners?

00:15:13.088 --> 00:15:16.049
There's a fresh episode of
Mandarin Orange is the New Chicken.

00:15:16.049 --> 00:15:18.635
Oh, thanks, Fry, but, uh,

00:15:18.635 --> 00:15:21.513
I'm going over to my parents tonight.
- Again?

00:15:21.513 --> 00:15:24.057
Well, my grandma needs
a lot of help these days.

00:15:24.057 --> 00:15:26.143
She fell and broke a few of her elbows.

00:15:26.143 --> 00:15:28.186
Okay. Well, see you tomorrow.

00:15:29.187 --> 00:15:31.732
I could go for a little Hulu and chill.

00:15:31.732 --> 00:15:33.025
You're on!

00:15:34.943 --> 00:15:37.070
Mm!

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:40.073
This twice-flushed pork is delicious.

00:15:40.073 --> 00:15:41.575
Leela, what's going on?

00:15:41.575 --> 00:15:43.952
You've been living with us
for six weeks now.

00:15:43.952 --> 00:15:45.746
I'm fine. I'm fine.

00:15:45.746 --> 00:15:48.332
There's just something that's... off.

00:15:48.332 --> 00:15:49.791
I can't quite...

00:15:49.791 --> 00:15:52.878
It's not my relationship with Fry,
if that's what you mean.

00:15:52.878 --> 00:15:56.048
- I didn't say--
- Maybe it's Bender. It could be Amy!

00:15:56.048 --> 00:15:59.927
- Is Fry upset that you've been away?
- No, he's fine with it.

00:15:59.927 --> 00:16:02.387
He's fine with everything. He's so great.

00:16:02.387 --> 00:16:03.722
I sure love him.

00:16:03.722 --> 00:16:05.307
I think I'll stay another week though.

00:16:06.683 --> 00:16:07.726
Mm!

00:16:07.726 --> 00:16:11.146
- Oh! I broke another one.

00:16:14.483 --> 00:16:16.485
First order of business.

00:16:16.485 --> 00:16:19.988
Has anybody noticed anything
weird around here lately?

00:16:19.988 --> 00:16:22.783
Yes! I was just saying to my parents

00:16:22.783 --> 00:16:24.534
that something seems off!

00:16:24.534 --> 00:16:26.954
I'm glad it's not just me.

00:16:26.954 --> 00:16:30.415
Hey! I just picked up some
four-dimensional pretzels. Have some!

00:16:33.669 --> 00:16:35.879
Mm! Tell me, Fry.

00:16:35.879 --> 00:16:38.757
Have you noticed anything strange lately?

00:16:38.757 --> 00:16:40.425
No. Like what?

00:16:40.425 --> 00:16:42.594
Well, for one thing,
these last few weeks,

00:16:42.594 --> 00:16:46.056
we've had an unexplained uptick
in worker productivity.

00:16:48.225 --> 00:16:50.352
While during the same period,

00:16:50.352 --> 00:16:53.397
we're using twice as much soap
in the men's room.

00:16:53.397 --> 00:16:55.524
I have noticed less body odor.

00:16:55.524 --> 00:16:56.775
- Oh definitely.
- Way less.

00:16:56.775 --> 00:17:00.237
It appears the changes
started six weeks ago,

00:17:00.237 --> 00:17:03.156
right after we delivered
that wedding cake.

00:17:04.408 --> 00:17:06.827
This is weird.
According to the ship's log,

00:17:06.827 --> 00:17:10.664
we made a detour to some
awful planet called Dalton-B.

00:17:10.664 --> 00:17:12.291
I don't remember that.

00:17:12.291 --> 00:17:14.710
Then, it must not have happened.
Good pretzels, right?

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:16.336
Wait. Dalton-B?

00:17:16.336 --> 00:17:19.339
Isn't that where we dumped
those liberry books 23 years ago?

00:17:19.339 --> 00:17:21.884
Yeah, and we had that temp with us!

00:17:21.884 --> 00:17:23.719
He didn't have a name, poor guy.

00:17:23.719 --> 00:17:25.429
Frank. His name was Frank!

00:17:25.429 --> 00:17:27.598
Oh, right. Whatever happened to him?

00:17:27.598 --> 00:17:29.224
Like I care, I don't.

00:17:29.224 --> 00:17:32.644
Something very strange
took place on Dalton-B.

00:17:32.644 --> 00:17:35.939
We've gotta get back there
and find out what. Right, Fry?

00:17:35.939 --> 00:17:37.941
Uh...

00:17:37.941 --> 00:17:39.568
Um...

00:17:48.911 --> 00:17:52.414
Yuck! This place is even grosser
than I remembered.

00:17:52.414 --> 00:17:55.250
And no sign of Frank.
Let's just go bowling.

00:17:55.250 --> 00:17:56.877
Oh, thank God you're here!

00:17:56.877 --> 00:17:58.921
You're just in time to see my beard!

00:17:58.921 --> 00:18:01.048
Keep away from us, you dirty hippie!

00:18:01.048 --> 00:18:03.425
There are no grooves here!

00:18:03.425 --> 00:18:05.010
We should leave this stranger alone.

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:06.970
He looks delusional.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:10.015
But, I'm Fry!
Don't you recognize me?

00:18:12.726 --> 00:18:15.312
You're not Fry. That's Fry!

00:18:15.312 --> 00:18:18.815
Yes... Fry...

00:18:20.651 --> 00:18:22.986
Leela, you know who I am, right?

00:18:22.986 --> 00:18:26.531
I do sense a familiar dopiness.

00:18:26.531 --> 00:18:27.574
No. No!

00:18:29.076 --> 00:18:32.746
He... is... Fry...

00:18:32.746 --> 00:18:35.415
No, I is Fry! And I can prove it!

00:18:35.415 --> 00:18:36.959
Here's a photo of me and Bender.

00:18:37.626 --> 00:18:39.920
That could be me with anyone stupid.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.505
I have a picture with everybody!

00:18:42.339 --> 00:18:44.341
I could never forget this one.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:50.764
You... You!

00:18:50.764 --> 00:18:53.892
I remember! You are Fry!

00:18:53.892 --> 00:18:55.435
Oh, Fry!

00:18:55.435 --> 00:18:59.064
If he's Fry, then who's the guy
with the spinny eyeballs?

00:19:01.358 --> 00:19:04.319
Alright, alright. I'm not Fry.

00:19:04.319 --> 00:19:05.445
I'm Frank!

00:19:05.445 --> 00:19:06.613
- Who?
- Say what?

00:19:06.613 --> 00:19:07.614
The temp!

00:19:07.614 --> 00:19:10.659
Who you stranded here
for 23 long years!

00:19:10.659 --> 00:19:12.160
Time flies.

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:15.205
Not here.
My only companions were the two books

00:19:15.205 --> 00:19:17.040
that weren't too moldy to read.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.750
I even built them a little house.

00:19:20.377 --> 00:19:22.546
The Art of Klang Foo.

00:19:22.546 --> 00:19:25.465
I must have read this a thousand times.

00:19:25.465 --> 00:19:26.967
And The Return of the King?

00:19:26.967 --> 00:19:29.261
That one I didn't read.
It's the third book of the trilogy,

00:19:29.261 --> 00:19:32.848
and I've never read the first two.
I didn't wanna spoil it, you know?

00:19:32.848 --> 00:19:34.016
What's Klang Foo?

00:19:34.016 --> 00:19:36.685
An ancient mind-control technique.

00:19:36.685 --> 00:19:38.854
And, oh, did I master it.

00:19:40.689 --> 00:19:42.983
- Cut it out.
- It was especially easy

00:19:42.983 --> 00:19:44.610
to pass myself off as Fry

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:47.321
because nobody can remember
who I really am anyway.

00:19:47.321 --> 00:19:49.907
But, why did you wanna take my place?

00:19:49.907 --> 00:19:52.326
Because you have such a great life!

00:19:52.326 --> 00:19:55.203
I've had so, so many temp jobs,

00:19:55.203 --> 00:19:58.373
but working at Planet Express
was the one time in my life

00:19:58.373 --> 00:19:59.875
I was truly happy.

00:19:59.875 --> 00:20:01.627
Whoa. Bleak.

00:20:01.627 --> 00:20:04.421
I loved it there, but my plan failed.

00:20:04.421 --> 00:20:06.715
So it's time for my backup plan.

00:20:06.715 --> 00:20:08.717
It better not involve the eye thing.

00:20:08.717 --> 00:20:11.303
- I'm going to abandon you all here

00:20:11.303 --> 00:20:13.222
the way you abandoned me!

00:20:13.222 --> 00:20:14.431
dramatic sting

00:20:14.431 --> 00:20:15.849
We've got to stop him!

00:20:15.849 --> 00:20:18.227
And by we, I mean you.

00:20:18.227 --> 00:20:20.229
I'm already in my pajamas.

00:20:21.271 --> 00:20:22.648
Oh. No, I'm not.

00:20:24.316 --> 00:20:26.360
- Oh, don't leave us!
- Stop!

00:20:31.907 --> 00:20:34.409
- Aah! I should've paid more attention

00:20:34.409 --> 00:20:36.370
that week I was a temp astronaut!

00:20:45.462 --> 00:20:47.381
Time for plan C.

00:20:47.381 --> 00:20:49.967
Kill everybody!

00:20:49.967 --> 00:20:52.386
That's not a plan!
You're just improvising!

00:20:54.513 --> 00:20:56.348
Now what?

00:20:56.348 --> 00:20:58.809
I have an idea,
but I have to warn you.

00:20:58.809 --> 00:21:00.435
It's completely brilliant.

00:21:01.353 --> 00:21:05.274
As you all know, my spice rack
is located in the ship's galley,

00:21:05.274 --> 00:21:07.150
and on that rack is a jar

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:10.445
of flaming hot
million Scoville chili powder.

00:21:10.445 --> 00:21:12.030
Ooh, that's the good stuff!

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.907
Using a light pastry shell,

00:21:13.907 --> 00:21:15.617
I'll bake the powder into a grenade

00:21:15.617 --> 00:21:18.370
to blind and disorient the enemy.

00:21:18.370 --> 00:21:21.623
Then, we'll launch it using
my party-size soup ladle.

00:21:25.544 --> 00:21:26.545
Questions?

00:21:26.545 --> 00:21:28.630
How are we supposed
to get into the ship?

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:30.507
What's-his-name is guarding the door.

00:21:30.507 --> 00:21:32.634
It might be possible to sneak in

00:21:32.634 --> 00:21:34.303
through the rear thrusters.

00:21:34.303 --> 00:21:37.389
Of course,
we'd be exposed to some radiation.

00:21:37.389 --> 00:21:38.891
How much radiation?

00:21:38.891 --> 00:21:40.100
Oh, not much.

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:42.895
Like having an affair with Marie Curie.

00:21:42.895 --> 00:21:45.772
Oh my, yes...

00:22:01.121 --> 00:22:02.164
We made it!

00:22:04.625 --> 00:22:07.169
Aha! My million Scoville chili powder!

00:22:07.169 --> 00:22:08.587
What's that for?

00:22:08.587 --> 00:22:11.381
I... think I was gonna
throw it at somebody.

00:22:11.381 --> 00:22:13.550
- Who?
- I can't remember.

00:22:13.550 --> 00:22:16.094
Hey, uh, why is the ship sideways?

00:22:16.094 --> 00:22:19.139
Who knows?
It just falls over sometimes.

00:22:19.139 --> 00:22:21.391
- Huh?

00:22:21.391 --> 00:22:23.644
No!

00:22:34.488 --> 00:22:37.282
Say, Fry, weren't you
about to go on vacation?

00:22:37.282 --> 00:22:40.494
I don't need a vacation.
I just had six weeks off.

00:22:40.494 --> 00:22:43.622
You did?
I could've sworn you were here,

00:22:43.622 --> 00:22:46.917
but I'm happy to dock your pay.
- That sounds fair.

00:22:46.917 --> 00:22:49.836
You know, I was kinda worn out before,

00:22:49.836 --> 00:22:53.131
but now everything feels... just right.

00:22:53.131 --> 00:22:54.591
Yes, it does.

00:22:54.591 --> 00:22:56.176
You wanna go home and have dinner?

00:22:59.346 --> 00:23:02.349
Uh, I think I'll eat
at my parents tonight.